ELTEC Eurocom E17 Linux port - status & plan
============================================

Base: the 030funtime MMU+device-tree line (setup_mm.c selects an
embedded DTB per machine; boards keep a small config.c for machine id,
early console and IRQ setup, while the DT drives the peripherals).
Modelled on MVME147 (the closest VME MMU board).

Hardware (reverse-engineered; see E17-NOTES.md in the qemu-e17 tree):
  MC68040/060, VMEbus, 0xfec00000 onboard I/O window.
  CD2401 serial (0xfec64000), Am79C900/LANCE (0xfec68000),
  NCR 53C720 SCSI (0xfec6c000), Z8536 CIO timers (0xfec10000/30000),
  M48T02 RTC/NVRAM (0xfec20000), VIC068A interrupt controller
  (0xfec01000), AT keyboard, onboard video.

Done
  - arch/m68k/dts/{mc68040.dtsi,eltec-e17.dts} (embedded DTB), validates.
  - arch/m68k/eltec/config.c: machine id, early polled CD2401 boot
    console, user-vector IRQ setup.
  - machine wiring: MACH_E17, VME_TYPE_E17, Kconfig ELTEC_E17,
    setup.h MACH_IS_E17, setup_mm.c dispatch + DTB fallback + bootinfo.
  - eltec-e17_defconfig; full vmlinux builds and links.

Boot status (tested in QEMU -M e17 -kernel vmlinux)
  *** Linux boots to userspace: "Run /init as init process" and the
  init binary runs. ***  With an embedded initramfs (CONFIG_INITRAMFS_
  SOURCE) the kernel goes through head.S, MMU/paging, DT unflatten,
  start_kernel, calibrate_delay, driver init (DT-bound M48T02 RTC,
  SCSI/NET stacks), frees initmem and execs /init.

  Fixes that got us here:
   - embedded-DTB pointer: use &symbol, not its first word; and the
     DTB must be page-aligned in embedded_dtbs.S (it followed
     mvme147.dtb at an odd address, so libfdt rejected it).
   - unflatten_device_tree() must run after paging_init() (memblock
     has no RAM before that) - reordered in setup_mm.c.
   - head.S: transparently map 0xe0000000-0xffffffff on the E17 so the
     onboard I/O window (CD2401 console, VIC, CIO) is reachable early.
   - system tick: eltec_e17_sched_init() drives Z8536 CIO CT3 (PCLK/HZ)
     routed through VIC LICR1 as a vectored IRQ on VEC_USER/IRQ_USER;
     calibrate_delay now passes.
   - the QEMU e17 machine builds an m68k bootinfo (MACH_E17, CPU/FPU/MMU
     68040, memchunk, cmdline) for -kernel.

Next (roughly in order)
  1. A real CD2401 console tty (mainline dropped cyclades) so init has
     stdin/stdout and an interactive shell works.  Today userspace has
     no /dev/console tty ("unable to open an initial console"); init
     writes to /dev/kmsg to be visible.  QEMU already raises CD2401 RX
     IRQs via VIC LIRQ6, so an interrupt-driven serial_core driver
     modelled on serial_mvme147_scc.c is the path.
  2. VIC068A irqchip driver so DT interrupts (LIRQ1=CIO tick,
     LIRQ6=CD2401, LANCE/SCSI) resolve via of_irq_get instead of the
     hand-programmed user-vector setup.
  3. -initrd support in the QEMU e17 machine (BI_RAMDISK) so a rootfs
     can be supplied without rebuilding the kernel.
  4. Root on real storage: LANCE and 53C720 have mainline drivers;
     bring them up (NFS root or SCSI disk).

SMP (the hard part - honest assessment)
  m68k Linux has NO SMP support today, and the dual-68040 has no
  hardware cache coherency between CPUs and no hardware IPI beyond the
  shared-DRAM + 0xfec58000 release we found.  Plan: bring the second
  CPU up as a controlled AP (reset vector at DRAM 0/4, release via
  0xfec58000 - proven with the qemu mailbox probe), then build the
  minimum SMP scaffolding (CAS-based spinlocks, per-cpu, an IPI over
  a VIC/shared-mem doorbell, explicit cache management at coherency
  points).  Full symmetric scheduling may not be reachable on this
  hardware; progress will be reported honestly as it goes.
